        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">I was playing The Sentinels against The Dreamer when Projected Paralysis came out. &nbsp;Since that card targets </span><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">&quot;The player with the most cards in play&quot;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">we had to stop the game for a bit to figure out which of The Sentinels cards count toward cards in play. &nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Ignoring things like ongoings, Is it:</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">The &quot;Sentinels&quot; team card + All&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">four hero cards?</span></p><p style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">The &quot;Sentinels&quot; team card + only the active hero&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">cards?</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">All four hero cards?</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Only the active hero cards?</span></p><p>We decided that all four hero cards counted towards cards in play, regardless of whether they were active or incapped, but that the team card didn&#39;t. &nbsp;Was that correct or should we have done that differently.</p><p>[I tried to search the forum for a ruling on this, but it&#39;s hard to use Sentinels as a search term.]</p>",
